1
00:00:00,190 --> 00:00:06,315
In 1958, a machine learned from examples.
It took fifty-four years to win.

2
00:00:06,675 --> 00:00:10,975
Rosenblatt's perceptron made
headlines. Then, in 1969,

3
00:00:11,025 --> 00:00:14,864
a book proved its limits, and
most of the field moved on.

4
00:00:15,104 --> 00:00:19,184
In 1986, backpropagation
trained deeper networks.

5
00:00:19,234 --> 00:00:21,224
But through the nineties
and two thousands,

6
00:00:21,274 --> 00:00:23,824
simpler methods were usually preferred.

7
00:00:24,154 --> 00:00:28,814
Then, in 2012, a network called
AlexNet won the ImageNet challenge:

8
00:00:28,864 --> 00:00:32,406
fifteen percent error, against
twenty-six for the runner-up.

9
00:00:32,726 --> 00:00:37,156
Ten years later came ChatGPT. The
whole story is on one timeline,

10
00:00:37,206 --> 00:00:41,695
every date with its source.
It's free, on OpenChronology.
